    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe front porch extension being 3m wide and 1m deep, with a maximum height of 2.8m that would be located adjacent to the dwellings existing front entrance way, as shown on the plans received on the 3rd August 2004 constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class D of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission.\r\n"
